ge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"While I don't think it's grammatically incorrect, I feel like keeping \"back up\" as a verb together allows it to be more easily recognized at a glance.\r\n\r\nIt looks like [the Merriam-Webster Dictionary also considers \"back up\" a single unified verb, which the subject (such as \"hard drive\" or \"project\") should go after](https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/backup):\r\n> **back up - verb**\r\n> ...\r\n> 3: to make a copy of (a computer file or data) to protect against accidental loss or corruption\r\n> > Be sure to back up your work.\r\n> \r\n> also : to make copies of all the files on (a device)\r\n> > a program that automatically backs up your hard drive","created_at":"2026-09-08T17:01:41Z","updated_at":"2026-09-08T17:01:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123297#discussion_r3960343565","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123297","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3960343565"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123297#discussion_r3960343565"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123297"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3960343565/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":1879,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3955745356,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"}]